# Handwritten Solutions

A local Agent Skill and CPU runtime for handwritten homework PDFs. An external
Agent reads the original problems, writes and checks English Markdown/LaTeX, and
calls the runtime. The runtime preserves top-level problem identities and creates
one page per problem, page PNGs, editable solutions and a provenance report.

This public distribution contains the stable CPU implementation and the licensed
Patrick Hand engineering font. It does not contain the developer's handwriting,
private research reports, personal models, or an approved neural/hybrid backend.
The package version is recorded in `pyproject.toml`; package contents do not imply
a new production release or author approval of a research candidate.

Use Python 3.12 or 3.13, Git and uv:

```sh
uv sync --locked --no-dev
uv run --frozen hwsol doctor
uv run --frozen hwsol render --manifest examples/phase2/mixed/job.json --workspace workspace
uv run --frozen hwsol workspace latest
# Verify the actual run path printed above:
uv run --frozen hwsol verify --job workspace/runs/<run_id> --pixels
```

Installing dependencies may need network access. Once installed, normal CPU
rendering needs neither a GPU nor Torch or model downloads. Use `--offline` with
uv when the locked dependencies are already cached. On Windows, executables are
under `.venv/Scripts`; on Linux/macOS they are under `.venv/bin`.

Install a Skill archive by unpacking its `handwritten-solutions` directory into
the Agent's skill directory, then follow [SKILL.md](SKILL.md). A wheel installs
the command line runtime; the Skill and editable examples accompany the source
and Skill archives. Native compatibility must be verified on the target machine;
the local Linux preflight does not establish macOS or Windows validation.

- [Job creation and output verification](public_docs/GUIDE.md)
- [Personal Profile and Studio workflow](public_docs/PROFILES.md)
- [Rendering options and explicit fallback](public_docs/RENDERING.md)
- [Workspace and immutable runs](public_docs/WORKSPACE.md)
- [Benchmark and experimental boundaries](public_docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARIES.md)
- [Licenses](public_docs/LICENSES.md) and [contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md)

Public archives are built from an explicit allowlist. Local instructions, project
handoffs, personal audit reports, samples and model weights remain outside them.
Git history is not a public distribution artifact: a clean source snapshot does
not establish that its ancestry is safe to share.
